# An allowlist, deliberately. Without this file the build context is ~94 MB of
# mostly node_modules — and it carries mcp/key.pem, the MCP Registry domain
# verification private key. .gitignore keeps that key out of git; Docker does
# not read .gitignore, so this file is the only thing keeping it out of the
# build daemon.

# Exclude everything...
*

# ...then re-admit exactly what the Dockerfile builds from.
!mcp/package.json
!mcp/package-lock.json
!mcp/tsconfig.json
!mcp/src
!mcp/LICENSE
!mcp/DATA-LICENSE.md

# Belt and braces. Last match wins, so no future `!` line above can re-admit a
# key, a dependency tree, or a stale local build.
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/node_modules
**/dist
.git
